    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Gunnar Henderson**, whose 83.29 score marks him as our premier offensive weapon. Facing Trey Yesavage, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a highly favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong platoon-adjusted projection against the right-handed starter. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** provides a reliable 80.24 anchor in the two-hole; while he faces a slight dynamic platoon disadvantage against Shane Baz, his elite recency and the projected hitter-friendly environment make him an essential play. We are also looking for **Coby Mayo** (62.86) to capitalize on the same matchup against Yesavage, where the park factors and SP skill metrics provide enough lift to comfortably clear our \"Strong\" start threshold despite a slight drag from his batting order position.\n\nThe scarcity of stolen bases dictates our approach to the remainder of the lineup, leading to a marginal but necessary start for **Nasim Nunez** (52.24). While his projected #9 spot in the lineup acts as a drag on his overall scoring potential, his speed profile remains a strategic priority for our category goals. The most difficult benching decision involved evaluating the depth of our reserves, though the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**\u2014due to either team off-days or injury designations\u2014largely simplified our rotation logic today. We are operating with a heavy reliance on the assumed lineups for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Coby Mayo**; should official lineups shift these players into lower-value slots, we may see further volatility in these efficiency scores. We continue to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Henry Bolte**, **Tommy White**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Franklin Arias**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we are maximizing our daily game caps effectively.",
